Template: debian-installer/rougarou-welcome/title
Type: text
Description: Begin Rougarou installation

Template: rougarou/welcome
Type: note
Description: ROUGAROU OS
 A quiet server. A capable operator. AI within reach.
 .
 Set up your location, network and operator account.
 Choose access permissions and optional tools, then review storage.
 .
 Debian server foundations and SSH are always installed.
 You choose your AI agent and container tools; neither is required.
 Connect GitHub and your AI provider after your first login.
 .
 Your shell is always available. Internet is optional for installation.

Template: debian-installer/rougarou-access/title
Type: text
Description: Choose operator access

Template: rougarou/operator-access
Type: select
Choices-C: headless, password
Choices: Headless operator, Password sudo
Default: headless
Description: How should ${OPERATOR} administer this server?
 Headless operator: sudo works without a password. This gives the operator
 and any AI or program they run full root access to the server.
 .
 Password sudo: administrative commands require the operator's password.
 Agents must ask you to authorize those commands.
 .
 SSH still requires authentication. Root SSH login stays disabled.
 You can change this choice later with rougarou access.

Template: rougarou/access-missing-owner
Type: error
Description: Create an operator account first
 Rougarou needs a regular operator account for SSH, AI and administration.
 Return to Set up users and passwords, then create the operator account.

Template: rougarou/access-title
Type: text
Description: ROUGAROU OS / Operator access

Template: debian-installer/rougarou-software/title
Type: text
Description: Choose agents and container tools

Template: rougarou/software-title
Type: text
Description: ROUGAROU OS / Make it yours

Template: rougarou/agent
Type: select
Choices-C: none, codex, opencode, gemini, claude
Choices: None / bring your own, Codex, OpenCode (download after login), Gemini CLI, Claude Code (download after login)
Default: none
Description: Which AI agent should be installed?
 Install only your chosen agent, or start with a plain server.
 Codex and Gemini CLI can be installed offline from this image.
 OpenCode and Claude Code use a verified download after your first login.
 .
 Connect your own account or provider after your first login.
 You can add an agent later; your shell always works without one.

Template: rougarou/docker
Type: select
Choices-C: none, rootless, system
Choices: No Docker, Rootless Docker, System Docker
Default: rootless
Description: How should this server run Docker?
 Rootless Docker runs under your operator account. Its tools are installed;
 start the user service when ready with rougarou-docker setup.
 .
 System Docker enables a root-owned daemon. Use sudo docker to manage it;
 the operator is not added to the privileged docker group.
 .
 Choose No Docker if you do not need it. Podman is a separate choice.

Template: rougarou/podman
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Install Podman?
 Podman runs containers without a persistent Docker daemon.
 Its rootless dependencies will be included. You can install it alongside
 Docker, or use it on its own.

Template: rougarou/herdr
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Install Herdr for managing agent sessions?
 Herdr is an optional terminal workspace for AI agents.
 It is separate from your selected agent and starts only when you run it.

Template: rougarou/stage-verify
Type: text
Description: Rougarou / 1 of 5 / Verifying installation media

Template: rougarou/stage-unpack
Type: text
Description: Rougarou / 2 of 5 / Preparing signed offline packages

Template: rougarou/stage-packages
Type: text
Description: Rougarou / 3 of 5 / Installing your selected tools

Template: rougarou/stage-configure
Type: text
Description: Rougarou / 4 of 5 / Configuring your server and operator access

Template: rougarou/stage-finish
Type: text
Description: Rougarou / 5 of 5 / Ready for your first login

Template: rougarou/install-error
Type: error
Description: Rougarou could not finish installation
 ${STAGE} failed. Your installation has not been marked complete.
 .
 Details are in /target/var/log/rougarou-install.log.
 Return to the installer menu to inspect the failure before rebooting.
